\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Not all the blood of beasts
\par On Jewish altars slain
\par Could give the guilty conscience peace
\par Or wash away our stain.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. But Christ, the heavenly Lamb,
\par Takes all our sins away;
\par A sacrifice of nobler name,
\par And richer blood, than they.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. My faith would lay her hand
\par On that meek head of Thine,
\par While as a penitent I stand,
\par And here confess my sin.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. My soul looks back to see
\par The burden Thou didst bear
\par When hanging on the accursed tree,
\par And knows her guilt was there.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Believing, we rejoice
\par To feel the curse remove;
\par We bless the Lamb with cheerful voice,
\par And trust His bleeding love.
\par 
\par \f1 
